+0. Install `@flowfuse/node-red-dashboard` (menu > Manage palette > Install; restart Node-RED) — v5.0.0’s dashboard items are Dashboard 2.0 nodes. The legacy dashboard at `/ui` is untouched. Ensure exactly one `ui-base` exists (default path `/dashboard`) and assign the imported "Update" page + notification nodes to it in the Dashboard 2.0 sidebar before deploying — the page then appears at `/dashboard/wp-update`.
+0b. If an earlier version (v3/v4.0) is already imported: delete that tab completely first (select tab > Delete; then Configuration Nodes > unused, remove the old WP Update `ui-page`/`ui-group` (and any old Dashboard 2.0 `ui-base`/`ui-theme` from a previous v5 import)) before importing the new JSON; node ids are unchanged, so double ids would clash.
+1. Import `update-tab.json` (menu > Import). A **WP Update** flow tab and an **Update** dashboard page appear at `/dashboard`. The deploy shows no warnings: the file nodes and notifications conform to the Dashboard 2.0 palette definitions. The file does **not** ship a `ui-base`/`ui-theme`: importing several Dashboard 2.0 tab files would place two `ui-base` nodes on `/dashboard`, and Dashboard 2.0 shares one socket server across bases — the second base’s pages get no live widget wiring (dead buttons). Instead: ensure exactly one `ui-base` exists (default path `/dashboard`; adding any ui-page from the palette auto-creates one), then assign this page — and each notification node’s `ui` field — to it in the editor’s Dashboard 2.0 sidebar, and deploy.
 2. In the dashboard, optionally set **Admin user/password** (only if the editor is protected with adminAuth; the token is fetched via `POST /auth/token` and kept session-only in memory). There is no Admin API URL field anymore (v4.8): the tab derives it server-side as `http://127.0.0.1:1880`, unless you set the `WPU_ADMIN_BASE` environment variable (required for a non-standard port or a non-empty `httpAdminRoot`, since a function node cannot read settings.js). Set **Backup directory** to `/data` if Node-RED runs in a Docker container, so backups and snapshots survive container recreation.
 2b. (v4.11+) No further imports needed: **Check for updates** also refreshes the **Tab status** field (one click, both checks); **Update tab** then keeps this tab itself current from this repo.
 3. Press **Check for updates**. If Available shows "26.5.1 (update!)": **Back up settings**, then **Update flow**. (The same click also refreshes the Tab status field.)
